didn't hear from a lot of them.

00:24:34.340 --> 00:24:37.910
And I was really offended. I was
like, I interviewed you at least

00:24:37.910 --> 00:24:41.750
tell me you know, yes or no or
something. And then one of them

00:24:41.750 --> 00:24:44.690
who works in the music industry
told me Oh, did you send the

00:24:44.690 --> 00:24:48.860
same format of message and I was
like, Yes. And he was like, Oh,

00:24:48.980 --> 00:24:53.300
well Facebook then will think
that you are a bot or a spammer

00:24:53.300 --> 00:24:56.750
of some kind, and then it will
send your message into the other

00:24:56.750 --> 00:24:59.840
folder, which could be you know,
the spam folder or the junk

00:24:59.840 --> 00:25:03.710
folder. Because they analyze
your behavior, and this is a,

00:25:03.710 --> 00:25:07.670
you know, a sequential activity
and with the same activity,

00:25:07.760 --> 00:25:11.120
maybe just change the name. So
that was something that

00:25:11.120 --> 00:25:16.190
triggered my my sort of thought
of like how these companies are

00:25:16.190 --> 00:25:20.540
making these kind of decisions
of which kind of behavior is

00:25:20.540 --> 00:25:23.750
legitimate, and which kind of
behavior is illegitimate, and

00:25:23.750 --> 00:25:26.390
then shapes our behavior
accordingly. Because what he

00:25:26.390 --> 00:25:30.170
told me that label manager is
that he, of course, has the same

00:25:30.170 --> 00:25:34.340
kind of messages, he changes
them in a way that will try to

00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:40.520
avoid this kind of being called
spammer. So, this, this was the

00:25:40.550 --> 00:25:43.940
sort of analyzing the internet
standards part. Here, I'm

